      "config": {
        "content": "Helio now returns a layoutVersion on panel create and batch responses, enabling the client to detect stale writes; lock ordering for multi‑panel writers has been unified into a single id‑ordered row lock, preventing deadlocks during dashboard updates. Reference checks were expanded to cover all registered step kinds, with preview coverage enforced and a shared reference‑check chain that rejects self‑referencing lanes and invalid join/union saves. UI improvements include blank categories rendered as “(blank)”, footnoted short chart cards remaining usable, and scatter pickers showing the “— None —” option only once; the editor now stops re‑saving step configs on blur and refreshes its schema‑drift baseline after mid‑submit deletes. Backend changes clean up orphaned resources: Auto Connectors are removed when a source creation fails or is deleted, pipeline runs are reaped via a heartbeat, and stored objects are deleted alongside their rows."
      },
